# A file under /assets/ that this release does not have (an old chunk a stale
# tab asks for after a deploy or a rollback) gets a plain 404, not the app's
# index.html with a 200 from the catch-all in netlify.toml. No cache rule
# matches it (the year-long one names each real file), so nothing keeps the
# 404 once the file exists again. Rules here run before netlify.toml's, and
# a rule without "!" never covers a file that exists.
/assets/*  /404.html  404
/agent /llms.txt 200
/agent.txt /llms.txt 200
/agent-context /curate-agent-context.md 200
/skills /guide 302
/skills/kleros-curate/references/* https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kleros/kleros-skills/master/kleros-curate/references/:splat 302
/skills/feedback/* https://raw.githubusercontent.com/kleros/kleros-skills/master/feedback/:splat 302
